  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Interesting Facts</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-body dark:text-muted">
    <li>MPF was introduced in Hong Kong in 2000, aggressively replacing the earlier ORSO system for the vast majority of employees across the territory.</li>
    <li>Mandatory MPF contributions are robustly deductible up to HK$18,000 per year for both the employee's portion and the employer's portion.</li>
    <li>Tax Deductible Voluntary Contributions (TVC) empower you to legally claim up to an astonishing HK$60,000 in additional tax deductions each and every year.</li>
    <li>MPF funds are strictly locked up until age 65, though early withdrawal is a legal right under highly specific circumstances, such as permanent departure from Hong Kong or terminal illness.</li>
  </ul>

